From 28ea94e2034c701c62db0ec4c516c658107f1b8e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 19:13:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] qml: the timecode card has Mode and Files, Files starts at
 Same as Mode

Why:
The timecode card had two rows, "UI timecode" and "File timecode", and
the second row always showed and set the clips' timecode on its own, so
a stock camera looked split even when nothing was set apart. Original
Apertar 1.6.0 has one row, "Mode", that sets both timecodes
(SettingsPage.qml:3766-3780). The split is new ground: Core records it
in UI.conf fileTimecodeSeparate, so the touch row can start at "the
same as Mode" and only show a fixed file value once the operator chose
one.

What:
The first row is "Mode" again. The second row is "Files" with the
options Same as Mode, Free Run and Rec Run. It shows Same as Mode while
fileTimecodeSeparate is false, else the bridge's fileTimecodeMode. A
fixed value calls applyFileTimecodeMode (target=files, Core writes
fileTimecodeSeparate=true). Same as Mode calls applyTimecodeMode with
the screen mode and no target, so Core sets both and writes false. The
row follows the key through SettingsBridge's UI.conf watcher, also
after a WebUI split. The Time of Day / Clip labels stay until their own
commit.

Tested:
check_ui.sh lane-ui1: PASS, 0 warnings (QML compiled ahead of time).
Nothing run on a screen here. On the camera, with the Core commits that
write fileTimecodeSeparate: Settings > Timecode, pick Files = Free Run,
then Same as Mode; grep fileTimecodeSeparate ~/.config/CinePi/UI.conf
goes true, then false, and the row shows the fixed value, then Same as
Mode. A WebUI change with target=files shows its value in the Files row.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NEFc1w7Y8dcyiV489BiwMr
---
 qml/SettingsPage.qml | 19 +++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/qml/SettingsPage.qml b/qml/SettingsPage.qml
index 811da2e..f3ddbb2 100644
--- a/qml/SettingsPage.qml
+++ b/qml/SettingsPage.qml
@@ -3981,7 +3981,7 @@ Item {
 
             InlineDropdownField {
                 width: parent.width
-                label: "UI timecode"
+                label: "Mode"
                 value: root.settingsState ? root.settingsState.timecodeMode : "Free Run"
                 displayValue: root.timecodeDisplayName(value)
                 options: root.timecodeChoices
@@ -4000,15 +4000,22 @@ Item {
 
             InlineDropdownField {
                 width: parent.width
-                label: "File timecode"
-                value: (typeof apertarControlBridge !== "undefined" && apertarControlBridge) ? apertarControlBridge.fileTimecodeMode : "Free Run"
-                displayValue: root.timecodeDisplayName(value)
-                options: root.timecodeChoices
+                label: "Files"
+                value: root.settingsState && root.settingsState.fileTimecodeSeparate
+                       && typeof apertarControlBridge !== "undefined" && apertarControlBridge
+                       ? apertarControlBridge.fileTimecodeMode : "Same as Mode"
+                displayValue: value === "Same as Mode" ? value : root.timecodeDisplayName(value)
+                options: ["Same as Mode"].concat(root.timecodeChoices)
                 openUpwards: true
                 popupParent: dropdownOverlay
                 dropdownController: sharedDropdownController
                 onValueSelected: function(v) {
-                    if (typeof apertarControlBridge !== "undefined" && apertarControlBridge)
+                    if (typeof apertarControlBridge === "undefined" || !apertarControlBridge)
+                        return
+                    // A fixed value sets the files apart; Same as Mode sends no target, so Core sets both again.
+                    if (v === "Same as Mode")
+                        apertarControlBridge.applyTimecodeMode(root.settingsState ? root.settingsState.timecodeMode : "Free Run")
+                    else
                         apertarControlBridge.applyFileTimecodeMode(v)
                 }
             }
